                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">About 100</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">No added sugar</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Premium</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Third-party tested (brand)</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p>
            Figures come from each label or listing at the time of writing and vary by flavor, so check the tub you buy. Price tiers reflect cost per gram of protein at typical retail prices. We ranked these on protein type, label analysis and certification status, not on our own test kitchen, and our <a href="/how-we-test/">how we test</a> page explains the method. Where we describe texture, we are reporting the food science of each protein type and what buyers consistently report.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. The Best Protein Powders for Baking, Ranked
